01:43:21.240 --> 01:43:22.860
I don't feel like we are lacking anything

01:43:22.860 --> 01:43:24.030
in our relationship.

01:43:24.030 --> 01:43:26.130
In terms of coastal health,
I'm down in parliament

01:43:26.130 --> 01:43:27.960
giving evidence on this next week

01:43:27.960 --> 01:43:29.310
and I'd really welcome the opportunity

01:43:29.310 --> 01:43:31.170
to create a coastal health network.

01:43:31.170 --> 01:43:33.090
There are challenges
in coastal communities

01:43:33.090 --> 01:43:34.260
that you don't find anywhere else

01:43:34.260 --> 01:43:37.740
and we need to highlight that
and change the conversation.

01:43:37.740 --> 01:43:39.480
Financial levers, actually, you know what?

01:43:39.480 --> 01:43:40.920
A lot of it's about relationship.

01:43:40.920 --> 01:43:42.810
When you've trained together
and you work in the same patch

01:43:42.810 --> 01:43:44.190
and you care about the same people,

01:43:44.190 --> 01:43:46.050
you find that people in
hospitals want to come out

01:43:46.050 --> 01:43:46.950
and work with you differently.

01:43:46.950 --> 01:43:48.600
So it doesn't necessarily need finance,

01:43:48.600 --> 01:43:49.850
it just needs friendship.

01:43:50.760 --> 01:43:52.800
I think there's something about addition.

01:43:52.800 --> 01:43:54.630
You're absolutely right
in terms of safeguarding

01:43:54.630 --> 01:43:55.920
and trip to ED here in Blackpool.

01:43:55.920 --> 01:43:57.870
We could talk about that over dinner.

01:43:57.870 --> 01:44:00.600
But in terms of the population
health leadership programmes,

01:44:00.600 --> 01:44:02.640
I do think we've created
something really beautiful

01:44:02.640 --> 01:44:03.660
and special here.

01:44:03.660 --> 01:44:05.970
I was teaching on the Global
Health Leadership Programme

01:44:05.970 --> 01:44:07.350
in Oxford a couple of weeks ago

01:44:07.350 --> 01:44:09.600
and health ministers from
