01:44:11.280 --> 01:44:13.140
our population health leadership programme

01:44:13.140 --> 01:44:16.170
across all of South America,
which is pretty exciting.

01:44:16.170 --> 01:44:17.400
Our relationship with the CVFSC,

01:44:17.400 --> 01:44:18.930
we can unpack that again over dinner,

01:44:18.930 --> 01:44:21.870
but it takes time and
lots of coffee drinking

01:44:21.870 --> 01:44:24.810
and really listening to
uncomfortable truths in,

01:44:24.810 --> 01:44:26.252
of what's going on in our communities

01:44:26.252 --> 01:44:29.370
and brokering different
kinds of relationships.

01:44:29.370 --> 01:44:31.500
Surrogate markers, I think if you study

01:44:31.500 --> 01:44:33.750
particularly the work in priority wards,

01:44:33.750 --> 01:44:36.180
you can make incredible
differences quite quickly

01:44:36.180 --> 01:44:37.740
and it doesn't have to take a long time.

01:44:37.740 --> 01:44:40.200
Some of this, it's about
focus care in the right way

01:44:40.200 --> 01:44:42.420
and making sure you work
with communities differently.

01:44:42.420 --> 01:44:44.160
And in terms of COPD,

01:44:44.160 --> 01:44:45.240
the answer to your question is yes,

01:44:45.240 --> 01:44:47.490
we've got some great programmes going on.

01:44:47.490 --> 01:44:51.450
- Can I, in the place of
"Strictly Come Dancing"

